seine (0.1-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add seine-oci-<release>-<hostarch> packages: prebuilt bootstrap,
    vendor and sbuild OCI images and chroots under /usr/share/seine/oci,
    imported into podman automatically instead of being built from
    scratch.
  * Add i386 to the imager's per-architecture tables (kernel package,
    hypervisor, appliance triplet), next to the amd64/arm64/armhf
    entries already there.
  * Only fetch the qemu-user-static interpreter a HostBootstrap really
    needs to cross-bootstrap another architecture, instead of the whole
    qemu-user package (~465MiB for every architecture QEMU supports).
    amd64 and i386, or arm64 and armhf, need no interpreter at all: the
    CPU already runs that code natively.
  * Fix pybuild installing seine's own Python code into a directory
    dh_install never packaged (debian/python3-seine, guessed from
    PYBUILD_NAME): seine.deb shipped no code at all until now.
  * Make seine Architecture: amd64 arm64 instead of all, and bundle
    the 'ai', 'tui' and 'test' extras' pip-only deps (litellm, textual,
    robotframework, ...) under /usr/share/seine/pylibs: none of them
    have a Debian package, so a plain apt install used to leave those
    features needing a hand-built venv. seine-oci-<release>-<hostarch>
    packages are now only built on a native (non-cross) run.

 -- Cedric Hombourger <chombourger@gmail.com>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 07:28:59 +0200

